# Cloudflare Durable Objects Rules (2025)

## What are Durable Objects

Durable Objects are stateful serverless functions that run for as long as needed, with built-in SQLite storage, WebSocket support, and guaranteed global uniqueness per ID.

### Key Features (2025)
- **Free Tier Available**: Now included in Workers Free plan (April 2025)
- **Built-in SQLite**: Embedded database with SQL Storage API (GA)
- **WebSocket Server**: Native WebSocket support for real-time apps
- **Global Uniqueness**: Only one instance per ID exists worldwide
- **Strong Consistency**: Atomic operations and transactional storage
- **Background Processing**: Alarms API for scheduled tasks
- **Hibernation**: Automatic sleep/wake for cost optimization
- **Session Affinity**: WebSocket connections stick to same instance

## Use Cases

- **Real-time Collaboration**: Chat rooms, collaborative editing (e.g., Google Docs)
- **Multiplayer Games**: Game state management with WebSocket updates
- **AI Agents**: Stateful AI agents with memory and coordination
- **Rate Limiting**: Per-user or per-IP rate limiters
- **Session Management**: User sessions with WebSocket connections
- **Live Dashboards**: Real-time analytics and monitoring
- **Queue Management**: FIFO queues with guaranteed ordering
- **Leader Election**: Distributed coordination and consensus

